The message undersells this one: it is not only the make depend churn.

Bridge_InstanceEvent gained Bridge_GuiProps, which carries every GUI_*
property on an instance out with the birth event as a "gui" object. That is
what lets a client know an instance's presentation annotations (GUI_Format,
GUI_Pattern) without opening an options panel - the surface that does not
exist when a control is just sitting on a canvas. The GUI_ prefix is the
whole rule: the engine stores these and never reads them, and no list of
blessed names exists in the bridge or anywhere else.

Also in here: src/dyn/bufftest.* and src/schedtest.* deleted, part of moving
the unit tests out of libframework.so and into the unit_test executable.

The dependency churn across every objects/*/Makefile is the make depend the
message refers to. It is noise; the two changes above are the content.
